            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to cremate, then the Tamil for a memorial meeting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ஓலைச்சுவடி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஓலைச்சுவடி — ōlaiccuvaṭi — \"a palm-leaf manuscript\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஈரம் பட்டால் ஓலைச்சுவடி கெட்டுவிடும். īram paṭṭāl ōlaiccuvaṭi keṭṭuviṭum. If damp gets to it, a palm-leaf manuscript is ruined."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural ஓலைச்சுவடிகள்; ஓலை, palm leaf + சுவடி, a bundle of leaves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஓலைச்சுவடி (ōlaiccuvaṭi) is a Tamil compound built from ஓலை, \"palm leaf, writing on a palm leaf\" (DEDR 1070), and சுவடி, \"a bound bundle of leaves\", whose origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
